Acceptance re-review after gap fixes (read-only; do not edit any file except the one result file named below) of tickets built on branch swarm/mini-board-split. For each ticket below, check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it actually met by the implementation, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Read the files; do not run anything. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-8007", "title": "Board project page stops flapping between Live and connecting; stream heartbeat", "files": ["tools/watch-assets/project.js", "tools/watch-assets/project-live.js", "tools/watch-server.mjs", "tools/watch-assets/app.js"], "acceptance": ["One owner of the Live chip on the project page; it shows connecting only after 2 missed polls or heartbeats.", "The event stream sends a ping comment about every 10 s so idle streams do not drop.", "Test: a fake slow read and a dropped heartbeat."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-mini-board-split2.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"codex","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket and one line entry per acceptance line. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test. Be strict and concrete.
